                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.24/504: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Trueblood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-20T17:00:00-06:00">September 20, 1943—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>656. In view of Department’s 598, September 17 [<hi rendition="#italic">18</hi>],
                    10 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">11 a.m.</hi>] Minister of Finance and Chief of
                    Country Agency, have accepted in principle the simplification of procedure
                    Alternative III and the OEW announcement may include Costa Rica among the
                    countries participating.</p>
                <p>Specific requests from the Country Agency concerning orders covered by Import
                    Recommendations and the preference to be granted goods considered essential will
                    follow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Trueblood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
